+---
+id: task-001-spring-newsletter-discount-codes
+type: task
+title: "Spring newsletter discount codes"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Spring newsletter discount codes
+
+The spring campaign sends discount codes in the newsletter. An order can take one code to reduce its items.
+
+## What it asks for
+
+- `SPRING10` takes 10 % off the order's items, rounded to the nearest cent (a half cent rounds up).
+- `WELCOME5` takes 5.00 € (500 cents) off the order's items, only on an order whose items come to 30.00 € (3000 cents)
+  or more.
+- An order takes one code at most; a second code replaces the first.
+- An unknown code, or `WELCOME5` on a smaller order, is refused with an error that says why, and the order is left as
+  it was.
+- The discount never touches shipping. Whether an order ships free is still decided on its items before any discount.
+- The order book offers `applyCode(orderNumber, code)`. An order's totals show the discount as `discountCents` (0
+  without a code), and `totalCents` is items minus discount plus shipping.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- Tests cover both codes, rounding of the 10 % (including the half-cent case), the 30.00 € threshold, replacing a code,
+  unknown codes, an unknown order, and that shipping is decided before the discount.
+- `npm test` passes.
